From: AD5X Open OS
Subject: [PATCH] fbdev: ingenic: no rotator setup without rotation on X2600

Probe always ran rot_ctrl_init() for the RDMA path, even at angle 0,
where the rotator is never started. On a cold X2600 touching the
rotator keeps the DPU from starting its TFT stage (by hand the rotator
writes hang the chip). Stock never uses the rotator. Only set it up
when a rotation is configured.

diff --git a/module_drivers/drivers/video/fbdev/ingenic/fb_stage_wip/ingenicfb.c b/module_drivers/drivers/video/fbdev/ingenic/fb_stage_wip/ingenicfb.c
index d49f68b2a..934ffb8c6 100644
--- a/module_drivers/drivers/video/fbdev/ingenic/fb_stage_wip/ingenicfb.c
+++ b/module_drivers/drivers/video/fbdev/ingenic/fb_stage_wip/ingenicfb.c
@@ -1466,7 +1466,12 @@ static int ingenicfb_do_probe(struct platform_device *pdev, struct lcd_panel *pa
 #ifdef CONFIG_ROT_INGENIC
 		if (fb->var.bits_per_pixel != 32) {
 			dev_err(&pdev->dev, "Rotate bits_per_pixel: %d failed,should be 32\n", fb->var.bits_per_pixel);
-		} else {
+		} else if (fbdev->rot_angle > 0) {
+			/*
+			 * AD5X: leave the rotator alone without rotation (as
+			 * stock): touching it on a cold X2600 hangs the chip
+			 * or keeps the DPU from ever starting its TFT stage.
+			 */
 			rot_ctrl_init(dctrl, 0, ROT_MODE_RDMA_MANUAL);
 		}
 #endif
